BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:IU La Casa Latino Cultural Center
DTSTART:20260923T230000Z
DTEND:20260924T000000Z
LOCATION:La Casa/Latino Cultural Center
GEO:39.168732;-86.525021
SUMMARY:Latine Indiana: Stories\, Roots\, and Legacy
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an engaging exploration of the history\, roots\, 
 and lived experiences of Latine communities in Indiana with Nicole Martin
 ez-LeGrand\, Multicultural Collections Curator in the Library and Archive
 s division at the Indiana Historical Society.  Martinez-LeGrand will shar
 e stories of the people\, families\, and communities who have shaped Indi
 ana's history\, highlighting their experiences\, contributions\, and endu
 ring legacies. Drawing from the Indiana Historical Society's collections 
 and her work documenting Indiana's diverse communities\, she will illumin
 ate the rich and often overlooked histories of Latine Hoosiers and the wa
 ys their stories are woven into the broader story of Indiana.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p data-olk-copy-source="MessageBody">  Join
  us for an engaging exploration of the history\, roots\, and lived experi
 ences of Latine communities in Indiana with Nicole Martinez-LeGrand\, Mul
 ticultural Collections Curator in the Library and Archives division at th
 e Indiana Historical Society.</p><p>  Martinez-LeGrand will share stories
  of the people\, families\, and communities who have shaped Indiana's his
 tory\, highlighting their experiences\, contributions\, and enduring lega
 cies. Drawing from the Indiana Historical Society's collections and her w
 ork documenting Indiana's diverse communities\, she will illuminate the r
 ich and often overlooked histories of Latine Hoosiers and the ways their 
 stories are woven into the broader story of Indiana.</p>
UID:20260923T230000Z-2382390@events.iu.edu
