BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:IU La Casa Latino Cultural Center
DTSTART:20261002T000000Z
DTEND:20261002T010000Z
LOCATION:The Back Door
GEO:39.165184;-86.534423
SUMMARY:Book Party: "Sadistic Cholas" by Olga Rodríguez-Ulloa
DESCRIPTION:Join us in celebrating the recent publication of Sadistic Cho
 las: Transfeminist Provocations in Contemporary Peru (University of Texas
  Press) by Olga Rodríguez-Ulloa\, Interim Director of the Latino Studies
  Program and Assistant Professor of English\, American Studies\, and Lati
 no Studies.Sadistic Cholas examines contemporary art and activism in Peru
  that reappropriate the racial slur "chola" as a site of political and ae
 sthetic intervention. Through a transfeminist lens\, Rodríguez-Ulloa exp
 lores how racialized women reclaim and transform the term to advance form
 s of political and aesthetic liberation.  Following a discussion of the b
 ook and Rodríguez-Ulloa's scholarship\, we'll celebrate with music and a
  festive gathering. This is a 21+ event.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Join us in celebrating the recent publi
 cation of <em>Sadistic Cholas: Transfeminist Provocations in Contemporary
  Peru</em> (University of Texas Press) by Olga Rodríguez-Ulloa\, Interim
  Director of the Latino Studies Program and Assistant Professor of Englis
 h\, American Studies\, and Latino Studies.</p><p><em>Sadistic Cholas</em>
  examines contemporary art and activism in Peru that reappropriate the ra
 cial slur "chola" as a site of political and aesthetic intervention. Thro
 ugh a transfeminist lens\, Rodríguez-Ulloa explores how racialized women
  reclaim and transform the term to advance forms of political and aesthet
 ic liberation.</p><p>  Following a discussion of the book and Rodríguez-
 Ulloa's scholarship\, we'll celebrate with music and a festive gathering.
  This is a 21+ event.</p>
